  "notes": "{立|た}てかける means to place something in a leaning position against a surface. It is a compound verb from {立|た}てる (to stand up) + かける (to hang/rest on).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- The person actively places the object\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n[object]を[surface]に{立|た}てかける\n- {傘|かさ}を{壁|かべ}に{立|た}てかける: to lean an umbrella against the wall\n- {梯子|はしご}を{木|き}に{立|た}てかける: to lean a ladder against a tree\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{立|た}てかけている / {立|た}てかけてある both describe the resulting state: something is leaning against a surface.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {立|た}てる: to stand something up (upright, not leaning)\n- {寄|よ}りかかる: to lean oneself against ({自動詞|じどうし}, intransitive)\n- {立|た}てかける implies the object leans at an angle, not standing straight",
